00:07:03.059 --> 00:07:08.631
and compositions. The waning moon will appear near Jupiter, Mars, and the bright star

00:07:08.631 --> 00:07:14.291
regulus in the eastern sky during the night of November 1st to 2nd, according to space.com.

00:07:14.851 --> 00:07:20.371
Observers can watch the grouping rise after sunset. The alignment puts three bright solar system

00:07:20.371 --> 00:07:25.951
objects together with a prominent first magnitude star. Clear skies after sunset will provide

00:07:25.951 --> 00:07:31.999
the best view toward the east. A decade-long collection of full moon images taken from sites across

00:07:31.999 --> 00:07:39.099
Italy, featured by NASA, shows the moon appearing brown-tinged gray when high overhead. Near the horizon,

00:07:39.319 --> 00:07:44.099
the moon often looks red or yellow because longer atmospheric paths scatter away blue light.

00:07:44.719 --> 00:07:50.639
Rare blue moons occur when larger dust particles are present. One image records the total lunar eclipse

00:07:50.639 --> 00:07:56.679
of July 2018, when the moon glowed faint red from sunlight refracted through Earth's atmosphere.

00:07:57.379 --> 00:08:02.739
The photographer documented every color variation over 10 years. Outside Earth's atmosphere,

00:08:02.959 --> 00:08:08.079
